# keel-nodebb: NodeBB of this image runs on Node.js line 24, the line that
# plan/main names (handbook note 0083, amendment of 2026-11-12). The lines
# conflict, so an apt install of keel-nodejs-26 would remove line 24 and
# stop NodeBB. This file keeps line 24 and refuses every other line.
#
# apt takes the first record that matches a package, so the record of
# line 24 comes first: updates of line 24 come with apt upgrade as usual.
# The second record gives every other name priority -1: apt has no
# candidate for it. dpkg -i does not read this file.
#
# To change the line on purpose, read "A change of the Node.js line" in
# the README of keel-nodebb: the new line passes commissioning first.
Package: keel-nodejs-24
Pin: version 24.*
Pin-Priority: 500

Package: keel-nodejs keel-nodejs-*
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: -1
